  "schema": "arena.voice-chains/1",
  "note": "Interaction chains (Ben, 2026-09-10): a spoken line invites replies from ROLES, each reply an atom from the replier's own library. The runner composes: opener -> hop 1 -> hop 2 ..., one line at a time, rolling first_hop_p * decay^(hop-1); a chain dies at max_hops or when the turn changes. Roles: target = the seat(s) the opener addressed (from the event), aggressor = the seat that caused the opener's grief, bystander = another voiced seat, leader = the highest-life other seat, origin = the chain's first speaker (hops >= 2). Nobody replies to themselves; nobody says the same line twice in a turn. Tuned after game 39: no single reply type may dominate — the bystander scoff was five openers' default and became a tic.",
